    <item rdf:about="http://alephnull.com/w/linux/axim?rev=1208628339&amp;do=diff">
        <dc:format>text/html</dc:format>
        <dc:date>2008-04-19T14:05:39-05:00</dc:date>
        <title>linux:axim</title>
        <link>http://alephnull.com/w/linux/axim?rev=1208628339&amp;do=diff</link>
        <description>*   Howto boot Linux.  This didn't work, but it appears outdated.  You put the initrd and the zImage on the DOS parition.  I got it to boot as far as the Tux, then it hung.
	*  The guys on #opie suggests another  Howto boot Linux
	*  The 40-pin connector  pinout.</description>
    </item>
    <item rdf:about="http://alephnull.com/w/linux/evo?rev=1241050459&amp;do=diff">
        <dc:format>text/html</dc:format>
        <dc:date>2009-04-29T20:14:19-05:00</dc:date>
        <title>linux:evo</title>
        <link>http://alephnull.com/w/linux/evo?rev=1241050459&amp;do=diff</link>
        <description>Introduction

The  Compaq Evo T30 is a thin client.  One day, while shopping at  Weird Stuff, I happened to pick up several of these for a great price.  About half didn't boot, but I think this is because they don't have a plugin memory card.  My goal is to install Linux on them.</description>
    </item>
